@page "/terms"
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Terms";
}

<article class="card measure stack">
    <h1>Terms</h1>
    <p class="muted small">This is a starting point. Edit it before you point anyone else at this app.</p>

    <h2>What you get</h2>
    <p class="small">
        An account that lets you write and publish posts to social platforms using credentials you
        supply. The service is provided as is, with no uptime promise.
    </p>

    <h2>What you agree to</h2>
    <ul class="small">
        <li>You own or are authorized to use every account you connect.</li>
        <li>You follow the terms of every platform you publish to. Their rules still apply to you.</li>
        <li>You do not use this to send spam, harassment, or anything illegal.</li>
        <li>You keep your own credentials secure and rotate them if they leak.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Liability</h2>
    <p class="small">
        Publishing can fail, be delayed, or partially succeed. You are responsible for checking
        that a post went out. There is no liability for missed, duplicated or failed posts.
    </p>

    <h2>Ending it</h2>
    <p class="small">
        You can delete your account at any time. The operator can suspend an account that is
        breaking these terms.
    </p>
</article>
